---
layout: changelog
title: "Sign users in with their Active Directory or OpenLDAP credentials"
date: 2026-11-17
cover: /images/blog/announcing-ldap-login/cover.avif
tags: auth, security
---

Users can now sign in to your app with the username and password from your LDAP directory, such as Active Directory or OpenLDAP. Connect your directory under **Settings** > **Identity servers** > **LDAP**, test the connection, and call `createLDAPSession()` from your app. The directory checks the password, so Appwrite never stores it.

Limit sign-in to the members of one group, map the attributes that hold each user's ID, email, name, and phone number, and keep accounts in step with the directory on every sign-in.

[LDAP login](/docs/products/auth/ldap) is available on Appwrite Cloud, and is coming to self-hosted Appwrite soon.

